earches (2005-2014) - Thesis/dissertation searches **Conclusion:** The September 2015 \\\"Pie Menus or Linear Menus, Which Is Better?\\\" paper appears to be Iram N. Khan's first peer-reviewed publication in the academic literature. **Note:** The email domain \\\".edu.salford.ac.uk\\\" typically indicates a student account, suggesting Iram N. Khan may have been a graduate student at the time. --- ### Step 4: Identification of \\\"The One That Had Authored Prior Papers\\\" **Clear Determination:** Pietro Murano is unambiguously \\\"the one that had authored prior papers\\\" as he is the only author of the 2015 paper with any publications before 2015. --- ### Step 5: Verification of Pietro Murano's First Paper **EARLIEST PUBLICATION IDENTIFIED AND VERIFIED:** **Title:** \\\"Effectiveness of Mapping Human-Oriented Information to Software Agents for Online Teaching Environments\\\" **Complete Details:** - **Author:** Pietro Murano (single author) - **Year:** 2000 - **Month:** September 2000 - **Conference:** Women's Engineering Society (WES) 73rd Annual Conference - **Conference Theme:** Human Interface With Machines - **Location:** UCLAN (University of Central Lancashire), UK - **Type:** Conference paper/presentation **Verification Process:** 1. Listed as the earliest publication on Pietro Murano's official publications page (pietromurano.org/publications.html) 2. DBLP database confirms no earlier publications (earliest indexed entries are from 2001) 3. Comprehensive searches across all major academic databases found no publications from 1999 or earlier 4. PhD thesis timeline (submitted 2009) confirms this 2000 paper was published during doctoral studies 5. His next publications were both in 2001, confirming the 2000 paper's chronological priority **Note on Database Coverage:** The 2000 WES paper is not indexed in DBLP, likely because the Women's Engineering Society conference is not a traditional computer science venue. However, it is clearly documented on his officia